// ODDLY TRUE v3 (owner 13 Nov: content 5/10 → STORY.md §3b; everything on screen a real model or reframed so it is not seen).
// Bespoke act x3_cook (engine/library/bank/cook-under-the-sea.js); generic figures, no likeness.
# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=open cam=EWS.high.drop tail=.25 amb=real_underwater
In 2013, a ship's cook was trapped at the bottom of the Atlantic for almost three days… and lived.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=loo cam=MS.eye.push lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_ship_interior
His name was Harrison Okene, and it all started with a trip to the toilet.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=flip cam=MS.eye.handheld lead=.05 tail=.1 amb=real_ship_interior
It was about five in the morning, twenty miles off Nigeria, when the tugboat rolled over.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=black cam=MS.low.handheld lead=.05 tail=.15 amb=real_air_pocket
The sea poured in, and everything went black.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=sink cam=EWS.high.crane lead=.05 tail=.15 amb=real_underwater
The boat sank upside down, thirty metres to the seabed.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=upside cam=MS.low.push lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_air_pocket
The toilet was now on the ceiling.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=corridor cam=MCU.eye.trackL lead=.05 tail=.15 amb=real_air_pocket
In his underwear, in total darkness, he felt his way along a flooded corridor.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=surface cam=CU.low.static lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_air_pocket
Then his head broke into air.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=cabin cam=WS.eye.orbit lead=.05 tail=.15 amb=real_air_pocket
A bubble just over a metre high, trapped in an engineer's cabin.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=rise cam=MS.low.static lead=.05 tail=.15 amb=real_air_pocket
But he was not safe. The water was cold, and it was rising.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=air cam=WS.high.push lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_air_pocket
And the air had a limit: about sixty hours, a physicist later worked out.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=torch cam=CU.high.push lead=.05 tail=.15 amb=real_air_pocket
He found a life vest with two small torches… and a single Coke.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=wreck cam=EWS.eye.push lead=.05 tail=.35 amb=real_underwater
Somewhere outside in the dark, eleven of his crewmates were already gone.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=eyes cam=ECU.eye.static lead=.05 tail=.3 amb=real_air_pocket
Alone in the bubble, he kept thinking about one person: his wife.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=eyes2 nocount=1 cam=CU.eye.static lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_air_pocket
The night before, she had sent him psalms to read. Now he said them in the dark.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=home cam=WS.eye.push lead=.05 tail=.3 amb=real_room_night
At home, she had no idea. She had lost her phone hours before the boat went down.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=eyes cam=ECU.eye.push count=1 lead=.05 tail=.3 amb=real_air_pocket
One day passed. Then a second.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=divers cam=WS.high.crane lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_underwater
On the third day, divers finally came down. But they were not looking for survivors.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=pass cam=MS.eye.orbit lead=.05 tail=.45 amb=real_air_pocket
They had come for the bodies, and the first diver swam right past him.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=hand cam=CU.eye.push lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_air_pocket
Okene reached into the light and grabbed the next diver's hand.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=alive cam=MCU.eye.handheld lead=.05 tail=.55 amb=real_air_pocket
"He's alive! He's alive!"

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=cabin nom=1 cam=WS.low.push lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_air_pocket
He had been breathing that bubble for almost sixty hours.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=chamber cam=MS.eye.push lead=.05 tail=.3 amb=real_chamber_hum
After three days in a decompression chamber, he said he would never go to sea again.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=career cam=WS.low.static lead=.05 tail=.35 amb=real_underwater
Two years later, he went back under it… as a commercial diver.

# vis kind=w act=x3_cook v=end cam=CU.eye.push lead=.1 tail=.8 amb=real_underwater
The man who waited in the dark for a diver's light now carries one.
